# Indexing for the Humanities.

**Authors:** Tibbo, Helen R.

## Abstract
Humanists use a wide variety of textual, graphic, and aural materials in their research, each of which presents indexing challenges. Research into the nature of these materials and humanists' information-seeking behaviors indicate that indexing models from the sciences are not adequate. New controlled vocabulary and indexing frameworks are needed. (Contains 112 references.) (Author/KRN)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ491446

